From 6fd7e22a8710b16bfbea231fe250e9b7014b6510 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:47:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: what the renders repeated, once

The three renders that draw a Dolby Vision picture (render_source(),
render() and render_hdr10()) each made the picture as libplacebo is given
it and the parameters they start from with the same lines, and nine places
of dvbridge_render.c and fourteen in six other files read the GL errors
that earlier work left with the same loop. Each time something was added to all
of them (the transfer of the base layer, the MMR table), it had to be
added three times, and one left out would not have shown in any test of
the others.

 - frame_for_render(): the source's planes with the colour of the
   metadata, no ICC profile or LUT of their own, and the enhancement layer
   with its chroma on the base layer's grid.
 - base_params(): libplacebo's defaults without peak detection, dithering,
   frame mixer, single-frame cache or border; the composer of CCM 001 as
   the renderer has it (on or off, the transfer of the base layer, the MMR
   table); where it says whether it composed; the step-down level. Each
   render adds its own: the source transport only composes, into its
   planes; the converted transport and the picture for HDR10 keep 32-bit
   intermediates; a plain picture has no base layer transfer and no
   step-down.
 - dvbridge_gl_drain_errors() (dvbridge_gl_pack.c): the one loop, used by
   the renderer, the packers, the copier, the import of the layer, the
   check of the bytes, the measurement and Dolby Vision as HDR10+.

Nothing else changes. Measured on Mesa's zink: fidbench in five
configurations, the measured test with the oracle of CCM 001 and the render
test with the composer and with libplacebo's reshaping give the same files
and lines as before this; with the MMR table of libplacebo-9977 asked for
and a mutation of it, the same as before this too, which differs from the
table's own (the switch still reaches libplacebo). The C files built with
-Wall -Wextra without a warning.
